@startuml
title User Registration and Role Granting
autonumber

actor "New User" as USR
participant "User" as U
participant "UserRoleProfile\n(abstract)" as URP
participant "LearnerProfile" as LP
participant "ContributorProfile" as CP
participant "ReviewerProfile" as RP

' (ClassDiagram – User.register)
USR -> U : register(emailOrPhone, password)
activate U
U --> USR : account created
deactivate U

note right of U
  GAP: displayName and arabicLevel are attributes on User,
  but no completeProfile()/setters exist.
  GAP: roleInterest attribute does not exist on User.
end note

' (ClassDiagram – User.addRole)
USR -> U : addRole(roleInterest)
activate U
U -> URP : <<create>>(role)
activate URP

alt role == LEARNER
    URP --> LP : <<instantiate>>
    activate LP
    LP --> U : learnerProfile
    deactivate LP
else role == CONTRIBUTOR
    URP --> CP : <<instantiate>>
    activate CP
    CP --> U : contributorProfile
    deactivate CP
else role == REVIEWER
    URP --> RP : <<instantiate>>
    activate RP
    RP --> U : reviewerProfile
    deactivate RP
end

deactivate URP
U --> USR : UserRoleProfile
deactivate U

note over USR, RP
  GAP: class diagram has no role-approval workflow.
  AdminProfile.manageUser(userId, action) is the closest,
  but "action" is a generic String.
  This diagram therefore models automatic role grant.
end note

@enduml
